.TH Path.move 3 2026-09-01 "Tomo man-pages"
.SH NAME
Path.move \- move a file or directory
.SH LIBRARY
Tomo Standard Library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BI Path.move\ :\ func(path:\ Path,\ dest:\ Path,\ overwrite:\ Bool\ =\ no\ ->\ Result)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Moves the file or directory from one location to another.


.SH ARGUMENTS

.TS
allbox;
lb lb lbx lb
l l l l.
Name	Type	Description	Default
path	Path	The path to move. 	-
dest	Path	The destination to move the path to. 	-
overwrite	Bool	Whether to permit overwriting the destination if it is an existing file or directory. 	no
.TE
.SH RETURN
Either `Success` or `Failure{reason}`.

.SH NOTES
With `overwrite=no`, the refusal and the move are a single operation the kernel performs indivisibly, so another process cannot slip a file into the destination in between. Moving a directory across filesystems is the one case that cannot be done that way and falls back to checking first.

.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
(./file.txt).move(/tmp/renamed.txt)!
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Tomo-Path (3)
